    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b9ad3e14216c2f08",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "a204812815f3da9ad5642fc2a7a17d081f9c1a28928201555b99507e29012305",
      "text": "After breakfast, meet your guide for a full-day excursion to the Argentine side of Iguazu National Park, whose trails and walkways offer a remarkably close view of the falls. Explore the Lower and Upper Circuits, then continue by ecological train to the Devil’s Throat, where the immense power of the water can be felt at close range.\n\nAfter the excursion, transfer to the airport for your flight to Buenos Aires; on arrival, meet your driver and transfer to your hotel. Known as the birthplace of tango, Buenos Aires combines European elegance with a distinctly Latin American spirit: a cosmopolitan city of grand boulevards, historic neighbourhoods, colourful streets and iconic landmarks, from the Casa Rosada and Plaza de Mayo to lively La Boca and elegant Puerto Madero.",
      "provenance": {
